goal: Continue the owner-requested cleanup and code-quality review across every project in E:\Source\Rust, including current-only SLM2, a real small working default through MiniModel.org and initial server seeds. Use docs/ecosystem-cleanup-2026-09-12.md for current scope and checkpoints; this goal is not complete at an audit or synthetic demonstration.

start:
  - Read workspace.uai, .uai/totem.uai, .uai/taboo.uai, the canonical memory, the report decision index, and the current Companion memory.
  - Verify root, branch, clean/known worktree state, remote equality, protected trees, frozen source/profile identities, and current test baseline.
  - Preserve every immutable historical operation, especially /10; create wholly new preregistered identities for real execution.

immediate_work:
  - Use workspace.uai current_companion_truth for implemented production acquisition, operation ownership, conversion, terminal inspection, transfer, listener and browser client wiring. Do not rebuild these from obsolete August handoff prose.
  - Continue remaining obsolete-code, model-artifact and experiment review. Preserve useful findings and compact identities before retirement; verify actual removals and keep blocked deletions explicit.
  - Establish an eligible exact source and fresh numerical bindings. The pinned Qwen3 source is rejected product ancestry; artifacts/ecosystem-cleanup-20260912/public-source-metadata-review.json records the reviewed public candidates and why neither is admitted yet.
  - The pinned training route still needs reviewed curriculum, independent holdout inputs and fresh exact program/environment bindings. Do not invent independent reviewers or reuse closed failed operations.
  - Prepare authorized MiniModel.org initial seeds from D:\LLMs\TinyRustLM after qualification; resolve the outstanding hosting placement decision before dependent changes. Default to eligible cache or a small qualified MiniModel download, keeping technical choices in Advanced.

ordered_gates:
  - Contract and hostile vectors.
  - Wholly new output-free registration and one-shot source operation.
  - Six-member semantic inspection.
  - Pinned source to scalar-native first divergence.
  - Optimized-native and real-browser-WASM parity.
  - Sealed source/quantized/browser behavioral qualification.
  - Exact peer import or explicit local conversion in product UI.
  - Fresh-profile multi-turn chat, exactly-once render, cancellation, privacy, and profile deletion.
  - Direct MemoryEndpoints agent coordination receipts and separate TinyRustLM.com Connect plugin login/continuity/cleanup receipts.
  - Package/site release, publication logs, synchronized documentation, deployment, rollback, and HTTPS readback.

hard_rules:
  - Source has one canonical repository per project; TinyRustLM model payloads belong only under D:\LLMs\TinyRustLM. Do not create backup checkouts, source copies or scattered scratch; use Git for history and retain only verified replacements.
  - No legacy, compatibility, migration, alias, fallback, repair, hidden retry, best-of-N, debt, test weakening, fabricated evidence, or counter inflation.
  - Keep model/raw evidence/credentials outside Git and private prompts out of public records.
  - Duplicate prelaunch memory only when every maintained copy stays current, secret-safe, provenance-labeled, and noncontradictory.
  - Commit and push each coherent green major change; deploy each affected site whenever its complete gate passes.
